# ============================================================================
# Nested platform layout (pacgate-ai/...)
#
# Added 2026-09-16 ahead of the C:\pacgate-ai-pr relocation. Git ignore
# patterns are ANCHORED to the .gitignore's own directory, so rules written
# for the old repo root would NOT have matched once the platform moved under
# pacgate-ai/. These repo-level rules are defense-in-depth; the platform's
# own .gitignore is relocated to pacgate-ai/.gitignore as the primary rule set.
#
# Without these, `git add -A` would stage ~1.9 GB of client data.
# ============================================================================

# Rust build artifacts (4.5 GB — regenerable)
pacgate-ai/target/
pacgate-ai/**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Client runtime data — conversation history, checkpoints, tenant DBs.
# NEVER commit: contains client chat history and credential material.
pacgate-ai/deploy/client-bundle/data/
pacgate-ai/deploy/client-bundle/.deer-flow-credentials

# Per-machine rendered config (contains API keys / secrets)
pacgate-ai/deploy/client-bundle/.env
pacgate-ai/deploy/client-bundle/deer-flow-extensions-config.json
pacgate-ai/deploy/**/.env

# OpenViking runtime state (per-machine)
pacgate-ai/deploy/client-bundle/openviking/ov.conf
pacgate-ai/deploy/client-bundle/openviking/ovcli.settings.conf
pacgate-ai/deploy/client-bundle/openviking/workspace/

# qm runtime state
pacgate-ai/deploy/qm-pacgate/tasks/
pacgate-ai/deploy/qm-pacgate/node_modules/

# Cloned upstream deer-flow source (regenerable from the git tag)
pacgate-ai/deploy/deer-flow-src/

# Generated build/delivery archives
pacgate-ai/deploy/*.zip
*.zip

# Graphify knowledge-graph output (regenerable)
pacgate-ai/graphify-out/
pacgate-ai/deploy/graphify-out/

# Integration test data (regenerated by cargo test)
pacgate-ai/pacgate-ai/crates/pacgate-api/data/

# Temp / scratch files
*.log
test-*.json
warmup*.json
graphify-ollama.log

# Credentials anywhere in the nested tree (belt-and-braces; the four known
# leaked files must never re-enter via the platform subtree)
**/pacgate-ai-remote-handbook/OPERATOR.md
**/MCP授权/法律数据库MCP.md
**/MCP授权/境外法律数据库和网站.md
**/百宸AI系统资源接入清单V2.docx

# The remote-access handbook is an OPERATOR-ONLY artifact by its own definition
# (its header advertises operator credentials). Excluding the whole directory
# closes three gaps the per-file rules leave open:
#   1. `render.py`  -- regenerates the handbook FROM the credential file, so it
#                      lives in the same trust boundary as the secret.
#   2. `pdf/*.pdf`  -- already tracked+public in the source repo, rendered from
#                      `step_*.md` sources that have since been DELETED, so their
#                      screenshots cannot be audited. A remote-access walkthrough
#                      plausibly shows live connection details.
#   3. future files -- any new step/asset added to the directory would otherwise
#                      be staged silently.
# Verified 2026-09-16: git check-ignore returns IGNORED for all four carriers at
# their post-move path; see runtime/relocate/ALL-CREDENTIAL-GATE.txt
**/pacgate-ai-remote-handbook/

# deer-flow is an EMBEDDED repo (122,116 files / 1,728 MB) delivered separately
# via `git push fork pacgate-layer`. Without this rule `git add -A` records it as
# a gitlink pointing at a commit that exists only on this machine -- a "phantom
# submodule" that any clone would materialise as an empty directory. Ignoring it
# keeps this monorepo self-contained and avoids a broken pointer.
# See runtime/relocate/STAGE-PREVIEW.txt
deer-flow/

# pacgate-ai-assets/ was the `pacgate-ai` submodule, moved aside during the
# relocation (it holds docs/assets for JZKK720/pacgate-ai, v0.1.0).
#
# DEFERRED DECISION -- intentionally NOT committed yet. Reason: it is itself a git
# repo, so `git add` would record a gitlink (another phantom submodule). Fully
# committing it would mean deleting its .git and thereby severing its connection
# to JZKK720/pacgate-ai + pacgate-ai/pacgate-ai. That is destructive and was not
# requested, so it is left as-is and ignored for now.
#
# Note: 43.4 MB of its 63 content files are 13 PDFs (41.8 MB) -- reference docs,
# not runtime dependencies. The 4 credential carriers inside it are already
# covered by the `**/` rules above.
# Revisit once the user decides: keep assets in their own repo, or absorb them.
# See runtime/relocate/ASSETS-STRUCTURE.txt
pacgate-ai-assets/
